            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The majority held that a straightforward reading of the plain language of \u00a7\u202f1983 requires that the unnecessary\u2011restraint and predischarge\u2011notice provisions of the FNHRA are enforceable under \u00a7\u202f1983."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 11,
              "start": 11
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The majority also declined to apply a broader interpretation of \u00a7\u202f1983, emphasizing the need for a plain\u2011language reading."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito; Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0003-0001",
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0005-0000",
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0000",
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0001",
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0003",
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0004",
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0005",
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0006",
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0007",
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0009",
              "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0010"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 71,
              "start": 32
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas, joined by Justice Alito, dissented, arguing that the FNHRA cannot be enforced through \u00a7\u202f1983 and that the spending power does not create private rights of action."
      }
    ],
